      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T20:25:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The comment that you added is just stating what the code does, which is already pretty clear from the code itself (the `memset`). The comment should address the \"why\": https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Implementation_Comment_Donts.\n\nEven though it\u0027s not required to do the memset in the older version of the code, let\u0027s go ahead and split this change into a separate CL. It won\u0027t hurt with the older code, and it will make the `git blame` history easier to understand in the future.\n\nI\u0027m still not sure I understand why this is needed after skimming https://boringssl-review.googlesource.com/c/boringssl/+/32004.\n\nIt looks like that change added a `memset` internally:\n\nbefore:\n\n```\n    gctx-\u003ectr \u003d\n        aes_ctr_set_key(\u0026gctx-\u003eks.ks, \u0026gctx-\u003egcm, NULL, key, ctx-\u003ekey_len);\n```\n\nafter:\n\n```\n    OPENSSL_memset(\u0026gctx-\u003egcm, 0, sizeof(gctx-\u003egcm));\n    gctx-\u003ectr \u003d aes_ctr_set_key(\u0026gctx-\u003eks.ks, \u0026gctx-\u003egcm.gcm_key, NULL, key,\n                                ctx-\u003ekey_len);\n```\n\nWhy do we need to also clear the context before passing it in?",
      "parentUuid": "0642029e_6f75a1fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 0,
