      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T20:47:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The original `CRYPTO_gcm128_init` would initialize the whole `GCM128_CONTEXT`.\n\nBut after that CL, `CRYPTO_gcm128_init_key` would only init the value of `\u0026ctx.gcm_key`. The other parts of the `ctx` still remain uninitialized.\n\nAnd passing the `ctx` that remain uninitialized parts into\n```\nCRYPTO_gcm128_setiv(\u0026ctx, \u0026aes_key, nonce, nonce_size);\nCRYPTO_gcm128_encrypt(\u0026ctx, \u0026aes_key, plaintext, encrypted_data,\n\t\t\t\t      plaintext_size);\nCRYPTO_gcm128_tag(\u0026ctx, tag, tag_size);\n```\nwill result undefined behavior.\n\nThe biggest problem is that boringssl didn\u0027t provide a proper way to \"init\" the GCM128_CONTEXT.\n(Because these are \"internal\" APIs, they didn\u0027t promise anything about the API stability, the code may need to be changed every time when we uprev the boringssl.)",
      "parentUuid": "591b5893_32f54cbe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 458,
        "endChar": 31
      },
