      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T07:22:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is, when building the boringssl, the toolchain file would not be able to know the path of EC repo, because the cmake is already chdir into boringssl directory(`~/chromiumos/src/third_party/boringssl/`).\n\nUsing the relative path to locate the file under the EC repo is not suitable, because we should support changing the boringssl dir.\n`make BORINGSSL_DIR\u003d~/src/boringssl BOARD\u003dbloonchipper`\n\nA way to workaround is passing the location of the EC repo into the cmake, but I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a better solution.\n\nAnd because the boringssl toolchain file needs to support gcc \u0026 clang at the same time. The common part only remains:\n```\nadd_compile_options(-flto)\nadd_link_options(-flto)\nadd_link_options(-lnosys)\n\nset(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE OFF)\n\nset(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PROGRAM NEVER)\nset(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_LIBRARY ONLY)\nset(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_INCLUDE ONLY)\nset(CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PACKAGE ONLY)\n```\n(gcc doesn\u0027t support -Oz)\n\nI don\u0027t see much benefit to share the common parts of config.",
      "parentUuid": "8220e97b_9cd464a4",
      "revId": "29c4c80b61082b2ec0abf28a03c628fd2fbdac04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
