      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:51:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e the boringssl toolchain file needs to support gcc \u0026 clang at the same time.\n\nLooks like we need to make `toolchain-armv7m.cmake` support both compilers too (originally I was testing with `clang`, but no reason not to support both).\n\n\u003e The problem is, when building the boringssl, the toolchain file would not be able to know the path of EC repo,\n\nCan you use `realpath`, like this: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3994291/47/third_party/rules.mk#63?\n\n\u003e The common part only remains\n\nFor flags that differ between `clang` and `gcc`, I think you can use https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/module/CheckCXXCompilerFlag.html or https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/module/CheckCCompilerFlag.html to determine whether it\u0027s supported and only add if it is.",
